# Applied by live-build with debconf-set-selections BEFORE package installation.
#
# "true" selects Debian's group-based layout for the capture helper dumpcap:
# group "wireshark" plus the file capabilities cap_net_admin and cap_net_raw,
# instead of root-only capture. By itself this answer is NOT a non-setuid
# configuration: when setcap is missing or fails, wireshark-common falls back to
# a set-user-id root dumpcap.
#
# The no-setuid, fail-closed policy for /usr/bin/dumpcap is enforced by the
# cham3-desktop package, not by this answer: a dpkg-statoverride plus a dpkg
# file trigger in its postinst stop the set-user-id fallback on install,
# upgrade and dpkg-reconfigure. If the capabilities cannot be set, capture by
# non-root users is unavailable; it never runs as set-user-id root.
#
# The image adds no user to the "wireshark" group. Membership is a deliberate
# per-user administrative step that lets that user capture packets.
wireshark-common wireshark-common/install-setuid boolean true
